---
description: ecoPortal calendar project constraints
alwaysApply: true
---

- specs/requirements.md is the product contract.
- Do not implement features outside the specification.
- Use React and strict TypeScript.
- Do not use any or suppress TypeScript errors.
- Do not install a calendar rendering library.
- Calendar views must be implemented by us.
- Keep date calculations and validation independent from React.
- Treat timestamps without timezone offsets as local time.
- Every behavioral change requires automated tests.
- Include negative and edge-case tests.
- Preserve keyboard accessibility and descriptive accessible names.
- Make small, focused changes.
- Before coding, explain which acceptance requirement is being implemented.
- Run the narrowest relevant tests after each change.
- Do not modify the specification merely to make tests pass.